# guard-b allowlist for donmai — same grammar as the engine's own header
# (scripts/guard-b-lint.sh), three or four ' :: '-separated fields:
#
#     <RULE_ID>[,<RULE_ID>...] :: <location-regex> :: <match-regex>[ :: <line-regex>]
#
# See scripts/guard-b-lint.sh for the full grammar and refusal rules.
#
# This repo's --all tree scan currently reports a large pre-existing residue
# (disclosed in the PR that introduced this guard, and in
# scripts/guard-b-lint.sh's own CI job) that predates guard-b and was never
# curated against it — the previous scripts/leak-guard.sh this replaces used a
# narrower rule set that missed it. That residue is NOT allowlisted here: an
# allowlist entry is an asserted, reviewed "this is legitimate," and asserting
# that at bulk without reading each hit would be worse than the residue itself.
# --all therefore runs report-only in CI for now (see .github/workflows/guard-b.yml)
# until it is curated file-by-file, the same way tui-components' and
# donmai-smokes' were. New content is still fully covered: self-test,
# --commits (this PR's own commits), --stdin (the squash message), and
# --commits (what just landed on main) all run BLOCKING.
#
# NOTE ON THE [BRACKETS]: this file is itself scanned, so any entry added here
# must spell a banned literal with one bracketed letter (`Rens[e]i`,
# `/api/cl[i]/`) — the same convention scripts/guard-b-lint.sh and its own
# .guard-allowlist use.
